cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use plspower, please cite it as below."
title: "plspower: A Monte Carlo simulation planner for PLS-SEM power analysis"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Briones
    given-names: Fritz Jeffry
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-3213-7623"
version: 0.8.2
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24291129
date-released: 2026-11-24
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/fritzbriones/plspower"
url: "https://01a1dfae-8fd9-812a-b8f2-f8ffdfb1f80c.share.connect.posit.cloud/"
abstract: >-
  Free web app for a priori sample-size planning in PLS-SEM. It estimates
  power by Monte Carlo simulation (PLS Mode A, path weighting, percentile
  bootstrap) for direct and indirect effects in models with up to three
  parallel or serial mediators, and finds the minimum N for a target power.
keywords:
  - PLS-SEM
  - power analysis
  - sample size
  - mediation
  - Monte Carlo simulation
